<title>INDONESIA: GE sees S.E.Asia revenues doubling by 2000.</title>
<headline>GE sees S.E.Asia revenues doubling by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Co's (GE) revenues in Southeast Asia should double by the turn of the century, a senior company official said on Thursday,</p>
<p>Kenneth Brown, GE's vice-president for Southeast Asia, told reporters that the multinational's revenues from the region amounted to $3.4 billion in 1996 out of global revenues of $80 billion.</p>
<p>He said the contribution to revenue from the region should double by the turn of the century. At the same time, revenues from Asia should be half of all GE's non-United States revenue, he said.</p>
<p>Currently, Asia's revenues are about 10 percent of worldwide revenues, he said.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
